course: dictionary
lesson: 14975
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word rendering is a good example. Look at the words around it before you decide.
explain: «Her rendering of the anthem made the whole hall sing along.» Here a rendering is a performance, or one person's version, of a song. The words anthem and sing tell you that.
explain: «The architect showed us a rendering of the new library.» Here a rendering is a picture that shows what something will look like. The words architect and showed tell you that.
explain: Rendering can also be a verb, a doing word, in the -ing form. «She is rendering help to the lost tourist» means she is giving help. When you are unsure, swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Rendering can be a noun (a rendering, renderings) or the -ing form of the verb render.
fact: A rendering can be a performance or version of a song, poem or piece of music.
fact: A rendering can be a drawing or computer picture that shows what something will look like.
fact: A rendering can be a translation into another language.
fact: In building, rendering is a layer of plaster or cement put on a wall.
exercise: «The architect showed us a rendering of the new library.» What is a rendering here? | *A picture showing what something will look like | A kind of school bag | A loud noise from the builders
exercise: «The wall needs new rendering before we paint it.» What is rendering on a wall? | A tall ladder | A window with a wooden frame | *A layer of plaster or cement
exercise: Lily says «rendering help» means giving help. Which meaning fits the verb? | *Giving help | Drawing a picture of help | Taking help away | Asking for help, politely
test: «Her rendering of the anthem made everyone sing along.» What does rendering mean in this sentence? | A computer error | *A performance or version of a song | A picture of a building | A layer of plaster on a wall
test: «The computer spent an hour rendering the 3D video.» What does rendering mean here? | Drawing it by hand with a pencil | *The process of making an image or video from data | Translating it into French | Covering it with plaster
exam: «The team translated the book, and their rendering in French was beautiful.» What does rendering mean here? | A layer of cement on a wall | *A translation into another language | A performance of a song | A picture of a new school
